comment.narrative:
•KNCHR-KICD partnership strengthened through capacity building of teachers on Global Citizenship Education integrating rights of intersex persons;

•A hundred (100) copies of a handbook on Global Citizen Education in Sec. Schools in Kenya printed for dissemination;

•Nine (9) public awareness & dissemination forums of the intersex task-force report’s findings held in Nairobi, Machakos, Kajiado, Narok, Murang’a, Kisii, Vihiga, Samburu and Turkana Counties;

•Knowledge of at least 270 State and Non-State actors on the rights of intersex persons built;

•Partnership created with State and Non-State actors on the protections and promotion of the rights of IPs.

•Eight (8) investigations conducted in Nairobi, Kiambu, Laikipia West, Migori, Isiolo, Molo, and Naivasha, including on rights of PWDs and other vulnerable group’s rights;

•One file submitted for possible judicial/Court action;

•Recommendations on appropriate resolution mechanisms of the investigated complaints made to the relevant duty bearers.

•375 complaints were processed across the KNCHR regions. 206 of these were admitted for various actions while 169 complaints were addressed through offering legal advice to the petitioners;

•236 of those complaints were by males complainants while 139 were by females and 7 related to intersex persons;

•Majority of the complaints (212) related to ECOSOC rights, 116 related to Civil Political Rights while 47 were on Group Rights;

•Eighteen (18) of the complaints (4.8%) of the total complaints received were by or relating to rights of PWDs (11 with physical disability, 3 psycho-social, 2 speech disorder, 1 visual and 1 with albinism);

•The top five rights categories were: Access to justice (55), Evictions (54), land rights (54), Labour rights (37) and lastly the right to healthy environment (34).

•Six (6) Strategic partners engagement forums held with partners in Moyale, Baringo,Elgeyo Marakwet, Embu, Murang’a and Kirinyaga and complaints referral partnership strengthened with over sixty partners;

•Four (4) Joint public complaints handling initiatives held in Nyamira, Laikipia, Thika & Makadara Huduma Centres and various LSK branches (Legal Awareness Week);

•At least 304 members of the public sensitized on human rights complaints processing, SGBV and other thematic issues.

•Two trial observations undertaken in two cases Nyahururu HC Criminal Murder Case No. 7 of 2020 and Isiolo Inquest No 3 of 2017;

•Advisory rendered to Court on infusion of HRs principles;

•A draft consultant’s report on monitoring County Laws on disabilities/PWDs rights reviewed.
